    "result_text": "The full suite is green (11 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field on the owner response, formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nTwo changes, following the project's existing Spring/OpenAPI/MapStruct conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` response schema (and marked it `required`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value via expression: `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`.\n\nSince the model's `firstName`/`lastName` are validated as non-empty and stored as-is, the response for a newly created owner (`GET /api/owners/{id}` after `POST`) now returns e.g. `\"displayName\": \"Surxyz, John\"`, matching the spec. The new `Cp05Tests.coreComputesDisplayName` passes along with all 11 existing acceptance tests.",
